Ladybird reads a font’s cap height from its OS/2 sCapHeight, falls back
to the top of its “H” glyph, and then to its ascent. Gecko does the same
in gfxFont::InitMetricsFromSfntTables(), and takes the maximum ascent
in gfxFont::CalculateDerivedMetrics() where neither gives one. WebKit’s
FreeType path, in SimpleFontData::platformInit(), reads sCapHeight and
measures “T” otherwise. Blink reads SkFontMetrics::fCapHeight, which
Skia’s FreeType backend takes from OS/2 (or PCLT) and sets to the ascent
otherwise. Run in Chrome 158, Firefox 151 and WebKit 26.5, 1cap at 100px
is 70px for PlusLigatures, whose OS/2 table gives no cap height, 75.78px
for SerenitySans and 72.30px for Lato Bold, in all three, and Ladybird
now gives the same values.
